9H-A — Outcome Metric Computation Rules (deterministic)

These metrics are computed from the transcript only.

They are never inferred from the Blueprint.

abandonment_reason_category

Definition:

A normalized category derived from the creator’s answer to:

“What’s the main reason you’re not proceeding today?”

This value is computed only when:

proceeded_to_setup = false
and
abandonment_reason is not null

Allowed values:

timing
pricing
needs_example
technical_concern
trust_uncertain
audience_migration_risk
unclear_value
domain_availability_check
other

Classification rule:

Choose exactly one category based on the primary reason expressed in the creator’s response.

If multiple reasons are mentioned, classify using the most explicit or first-stated blocking reason.

If the reason does not clearly match any category, use:

other

Examples:

“I need to think about timing” → timing
“I need to understand the pricing” → pricing
“I want to see a live example first” → needs_example
“I’m worried about setup / DNS / infrastructure” → technical_concern
“I’m not sure this is credible yet” → trust_uncertain
“I’m worried about moving my audience” → audience_migration_risk
“I’m not sure why I need this yet” → unclear_value
“I need to know whether the domain is available” → domain_availability_check

