14A — Diagnostic Transcript JSON Schema

Diagnostic Transcript Object

The Diagnostic Transcript captures the full decision log of the onboarding session.

It is used for:

• debugging
• flow tuning
• analytics verification
• training data for improving recommendations

This object must contain only structured data.

It must not contain regenerated text.

It must reflect exactly what occurred during the session.

diagnostic_transcript {

  flow_version

  session_start_timestamp

  steps [

    {
      step_id
      step_name

      options_generated

      recommended_option

      creator_response

      final_selection

      iteration_index
    }

  ]

}

Field Definitions

"flow_version": "commonshub_onboarding_v1"

session_start_timestamp

ISO-8601 timestamp when the onboarding session began.

Example: 

2026-03-12T16:02:31Z

steps

Array containing each decision step.

Steps included:

step_1_positioning
step_2_community_name
step_3_domain
step_4_header_line
step_5_owner_profile

Micro-intake is not included.

⸻

step_id

Canonical identifier.

Example:

step_2_community_name

step_name

Human readable label.

Example:

Community Name

options_generated

Array of the options shown to the creator.

Example

[
"The Security Brief",
"The Strategic Signal",
"The Ukraine Briefing Room"
]

If the step regenerated options, each iteration must appear as a separate step object.

⸻

recommended_option

Exact text of the option recommended by the system.

Example

"The Security Brief"

creator_response

Exact response given by the creator.

Examples

"approve"
"Option B"
"My final: Strategic Signal"

final_selection

The approved value that was locked.

Example

"The Security Brief"

iteration_index

Indicates which generation cycle the step represents.

First generation:

0

First regeneration:

1

Second regeneration:

2

